  "blocking_reason": "Tohseno 1.2.0 release candidate 6 was built from exact clean and fully CI-gated commit fddab7d, Developer ID signed, Apple-notarized under submission be3cb4d7-16dc-40cb-9a09-2505ad0be7b9, stapled, mounted, Gatekeeper-verified, published as an immutable GitHub prerelease, origin-verified, and activated on tohseno.com's release-candidate channel with digest 082c9d1c8e44574cdb48132753e243c372ab21b675674527c0391589af7df2de. RC1 is rejected because its bundle omitted the Apple identity source package required for Companion dependency resolution; RC2 is rejected because owner-attended first-open acceptance found that it did not welcome or explain the system before technical setup; RC3 is rejected because the Mac app rejected valid Registry responses and did not expose the CLI activation and Ship path; RC4 is rejected because its CLI timed out while Xcode correctly continued a real adoption build; RC5 is rejected because its scanner mistook a short byte prefix inside compressed PNG data for a complete credential. Dedicated Registry and Claims relayers are funded but disabled outside the owner-attended acceptance window. RC6 deploy is now blocked only until the paired iPhone opens Companion and announces its non-exportable Builder DeviceKey to the Mac. Stable promotion remains blocked until the owner-attended physical acceptance completes one real Ship and immutable edition, a second identity's physical Claim and canonical receipt, offline-Mac exact-release preparation, recipient-local signed iPhone install, later Update preservation, private Follow reconciliation, live receipt/metadata verification, and exactly one Ship in the public timeline."
